<body>
  <h2>ABSTRACT</h2>
  <p><b>Background:</b> The beauty and luxury grooming industry has rapidly expanded, yet salon management largely suffers from fragmented operations, manual appointment booking, disconnected product retail, and limited operational transparency. Operating a modern salon requires coordinating client preferences, stylist schedules, waitlists, service durations, billing, and retail inventory. A unified web platform that systematically integrates client scheduling, administrative staff management, e-commerce retail, and order logistics provides an efficient digital transformation pathway for salon enterprises.</p>
  <p><b>Purpose:</b> The project aimed to design and implement "Luxe Groom," a comprehensive, multi-portal salon management and e-commerce system. The system seeks to eliminate appointment scheduling conflicts, streamline salon workforce management, enable direct-to-consumer grooming product retail, and provide real-time order tracking and dispatch for delivery personnel, demonstrating how modern full-stack web architectures optimize service-oriented business workflows.</p>
  <p><b>Methodology:</b> A full-stack software engineering and system implementation methodology was employed using the MERN stack (MongoDB, Express.js, React 19, and Node.js) bundled with Vite and Tailwind CSS. The architecture comprises three dedicated portals: a Customer Booking and E-Commerce Portal, an Admin and Staff Operations Dashboard, and a Delivery Personnel GIS Dashboard. Real-time bidirectional communication was established via Socket.io for live appointment alerts and delivery updates. The system incorporates Haversine geospatial calculations centered in Udupi to compute delivery fees and boundaries, Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) via JWT and bcrypt authentication, dynamic slot-locking algorithms to prevent overlapping stylist bookings, and automated PDF invoice generation. System performance, transactional integrity, and responsiveness were evaluated across realistic salon operational scenarios.</p>
  <p><b>Finding/Result:</b> The implemented platform achieved seamless synchronization across all three portals with sub-200ms API response latency and zero scheduling conflicts during concurrent booking simulations. Key salon workflows—including multi-service appointment scheduling, dynamic stylist allocation, staff attendance and leave management, digital wallet loyalty credits, personalized coupon discounts, and Leaflet-based GPS delivery routing—were successfully verified. The findings demonstrate that a decoupled, multi-portal architecture significantly reduces administrative overhead and enhances customer booking convenience and order visibility.</p>
  <p><b>Originality/Value:</b> The project provides a unified, production-ready solution that bridges salon appointment management with an integrated retail e-commerce and delivery ecosystem. Unlike conventional generic scheduling tools or isolated online stores, Luxe Groom demonstrates how specialized role-based interfaces, real-time event-driven updates, and geospatial logistics can be converged into a single cohesive progressive web application for modern salon management.</p>
  <p><b>Paper Type:</b> Software Engineering and System Implementation Study.</p>
  <p><b>Keywords:</b> Salon management system, appointment scheduling, MERN stack, e-commerce, real-time web applications, Socket.io, role-based access control, Leaflet GIS, delivery tracking, Luxe Groom, Udupi.</p>
</body>
